==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[File:Psetta maxima Luc Viatour.jpg|thumb|''Scophthalmus maximus'']]

===Etymology===
From Old (and modern) {{etyl|fr|en}} ''[[turbot#French|turbot]]'', from {{etyl|gmq-osw|en}} ''[[tornbut]]'', from ''[[törn]]'' (“thorn”) + ''[[but]]'' (“butt, flatfish”).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈtɜːbət/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|turbot|turbots}}

# A species of [[flatfish]] native to Europe, ''Scophthalmus maximus'', earlier ''Psetta maxima''.
# Any of various other [[flatfish]]es of family ''{{l|mul|Scophthalmidae}}'' that are found in marine or brackish waters.
#*{{quote-book|year=1931|author=[[w:John Palmer (author)|Francis Beeding]]
|title=Death Walks in Eastrepps
|chapter=1/1|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL6342782W
|passage=Eldridge closed the despatch-case with a snap and, rising briskly, walked down the corridor to his solitary table in the dining-car. Mulligatawny soup, poached '''turbot''', roast leg of lamb—the usual railway dinner.}}
# [[triggerfish|Triggerfish]], {{taxlink}Canthidermis sufflamen|species|noshow=1}}.

